 original `sorry`.\n\n- **Formally Verified Helper Lemmas in Lean 4 (checked with exit code 0 via `check.sh`)**:\n  1. `scratch.lean`:\n     - `minUpTo_le`: `minUpTo n p ≤ k` given `k ≤ n` and `p k`.\n     - `radius_le_eccentricity`: `GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v` for any vertex `v`.\n     - `le_romanDominationNumber`: Shows `(∀ f, IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → k ≤ romanWeight f) → k ≤ romanDominationNumber G`.\n  2. `test_ball.lean`:\n     - `self_mem_ballWithin`: `v ∈ ballWithin G k v`.\n     - `ballWithin_subset_succ`: `ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) v`.\n     - `adj_mem_ballWithin_succ`: `u ∈ ballWithin G k v → G.Adj u w → w ∈ ballWithin G (k + 1) v`.\n     - `ballWithin_trans`: `u ∈ ballWithin G k v → w ∈ ballWithin G m u → w ∈ ballWithin G (k + m) v`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Technical Constraints\n- **Lean 4 / check.sh Constraints**:\n  - `check.sh` runs `antigravity_handoff.py lint` which strictly forbids `variable`, `namespace`, `section`, `axiom`, `native_decide`, and any token matching `_FORBIDDEN_CMD` or `_FORBIDDEN_TOKEN`.\n  - All lemma parameters must be explicitly bound: `{V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]`.\n  - In `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`, line 15 currently has a dummy `lemma test_helper : 1 + 1 = 2 := rfl`. Helper lemmas should replace or follow this before `theorem prove_e20263a9`.\n  - `refute_e20263a9` must preserve its exact pristine string:\n    ```lean\n    theorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate := by\n      sorry\n    ```\n- **Proof Structure for `Candidate`**:\n  Using `le_romanDominationNumber`, it suffices to show:\n  ```lean\n  ∀ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f\n  ```\n  Since `GraphCalc.HasRadius G` guarantees `∀ v, ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v = univ`, by `minUpTo_le` we have `GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ Fintype.card V`, and therefore `GraphCalc.radius G ≤ Fintype.card V`.\n  If `Fintype.card V + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`, the inequality is immediately `radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`.\n  For the case where `romanWeight f ≤ Fintype.card V`, there exists at least one vertex $u$ with $f(u) = 2$ dominating its neighborhood, allowing eccentricity to be bounded by $W - 1$.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Active Subagents**:\n  - Blackboard Updater: `18016336-8199-4b18-961d-8bc9b578f414` (idle).\n  - Worker 4: `0d77a839-cb15-4b7b-9247-e4cbcb2ae788` (task-98 running nonisomorphic trees check; can be killed/messaged).\n  - Worker 5: `7841936c-55c7-41c5-92b8-9773cb8ee932` (active, explored Mathlib and verified `test_ball.lean`).\n- **Workspace State**:\n  - `scratch.lean` and `test_ball.lean` contain working, verified lemmas.\n  - Target `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` has not yet been edited with the final proof.\n- **Spawn Count**: 5 / 16 (Succession threshold is 16).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Combine Verified Lemmas into `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`**:\n   - Merge `minUpTo_le`, `radius_le_eccentricity`, `le_romanDominationNumber` (from `scratch.lean`) and `self_mem_ballWithin`, `ballWithin_subset_succ`, `adj_mem_ballWithin_succ`, `ballWithin_trans` (from `test_ball.lean`) into `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` right after line 14 (replacing `lemma test_helper`).\n2. **Complete the Proof of `prove_e20263a9`**:\n   - Fill in `theorem prove_e20263a9 : Candidate := by ...` using the helper lemmas to establish `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G`.\n   - Ensure `theorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate := by sorry` remains untouched.\n3. **Verify with `check.sh`**:\n   - Instruct Worker 5 (or run via follower) `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean`.\n   - Confirm exit code 0 and output: `CHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.` with only `refute_e20263a9` containing `sorryAx`.\n4. **Trigger Synthesis & Deliver**:\n   - Send `\"Synthesis started.\"` 